module examples.err_mmio_not_lowered

# plans/M7.md item C's honest boundary, pinned rather than described: a
# typed MMIO access type-checks in full (`golden/check-mmio-access`) and
# then stops at the backend, by name.
#
# The reason is not that lowering is hard. It is that **no `Mmio[L]` value
# exists at runtime yet**, so there is no base address to access, and any
# emitted load/store would run against whatever a zero-filled field
# happens to hold. Two independent blockers, both outside item C:
#
#   1. `eval::image_checks::check_capability_substitution` rejects an
#      `Mmio[L]` `init` parameter outright ("nothing mints a `Mmio` yet").
#      That is the mint.
#   2. `layout::build_boot_init_calls` walks `graph.actors` only — a
#      `@driver`'s `init` is never called at boot at all — and fails
#      closed on every capability parameter besides. So no capability of
#      any kind has bytes at boot today, `DeviceCap[D]` included.
#
# plans/M7.md item W is why this is a rejection instead of emitted code:
# an image that booted, asserted and reported success against a field
# that was never materialized is a wrong answer, not a missing feature.
# When the mint lands, this expectation is what has to change.

@layout(mmio, endian=little)
struct VirtioIrqMmio:
    @offset(0x060) interrupt_status: ReadOnly[u32]

@driver
pub struct BlkDriver:
    irq_regs: Mmio[VirtioIrqMmio]

    fn poll(read self) -> u32:
        return self.irq_regs.interrupt_status.read()
